// ------------------------------------------------------------
//  Rozdział osiemnasty — Wybór. We wsi trzecie łuczywo gaśnie o świcie.
//  W sercu boru ze szczeliny w dębie wychodzi kilkanaście Marysi — kopie odbite
//  na opak, bez cienia, które nie płaczą i śpiewają melodię do końca.
//  Jeden dotyk: imię (źle), melodia (dobrze), buzie (dobrze, przy ubraniu na
//  lewą stronę źle), drewniak (źle), skarb z bazy (dobrze), cień (dobrze po
//  pytaniu o Marysię, źle przy cieniu w zastawie), pies, Franek (dobrze, z ceną).
//  Dobry wybór: Marysia płacze, wraca do domu. Zły: dziecko stygnie na skraju
//  młodnika — „pochowasz je jak swoje”. Pan Lasu zapowiada Zaduszki.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

=== rozdzial_osiemnasty ===
# tlo: izba_swit
# rozdzial: Chapter Eighteen
# tytul: The Choice
The third pine splint in as many nights was burning down in the window that faced the forest. Hanka had come back from the edge of the young wood before dawn and, for the first time since Midsummer Night, had fallen asleep beside it—her head on the sill—and never felt the flame go out or the grey of daybreak seep into the room. She was woken by the cock at Staś’s. She started up, looked at the cold, charred stub and screamed so that Antek, who had slept on hay in the passage these three nights, burst in barefoot. # pokaz: antek
“It’s gone out,” she kept saying, raking through the ashes with her fingers. “It went out while I slept.” And then she flung the window wide, leaned out towards the forest and began the lullaby all over again, from the very first word, louder than on any of the three nights, {pani_w_zbozu_noc == za_spiewem:in that cracked whisper of hers that tore at her throat|until her voice carried far out over the young wood}.
Beyond the window the mist lay on the swathes like a crumpled sheet. The first men were already making for the meadows with their rakes—and they stopped short, hearing from Jaromir’s window the lullaby that Hanka was sending towards the forest.
{ dlug_u_jagny:
    Jagna, who had spent the night in her cart by the fence, got up, brushed the dry flecks of St John’s wort from her skirt and said only, “Today.” She did not explain what she meant.
}
Antek struck a light for a fresh splint. For a long while the spark would not catch the tinder. When at last it took flame, Hanka did not break off the lullaby, but held her hand over the fire until it scorched her—the way one shields something that must not be lost again. # pokaz: luczywo # dalej
-> dzieci_spod_debu

= dzieci_spod_debu
# tlo: dzieci_debu
In the heart of the forest the dawn did not come from the east. It seeped in from everywhere, grey and chill as ash from a stove gone cold, and there was not a single bird’s voice in it.
{ zastaw_u_leszego == zastaw_siekiera:
    Jaromir reached for his belt without thinking. His hand met emptiness, and for a long while would not come away.
}
{ zastaw_u_leszego == zastaw_krzesiwo:
    His hands were still numb, as though what he had left in the hollow was not the flint and steel but all his warmth.
}
{ wejscie_do_boru == ubranie_na_lewo:
    The oak that had stood at his right hand in the evening now stood at his left, though it had not moved from its place.
}
The Lord of the Forest stepped up to the oak and laid his palm on the cleft in the trunk. The bark parted with a soft crack, like bread being broken, and out of it, one after another, little girls began to come. # pokaz: dzieci
White shifts. Red ribbons in their hair. Bare feet, freckles on their noses. More than a dozen of them—each one a little Marysia—came out onto the lichen and sat down in a ring, shoulder to shoulder, small hands folded in their laps, like dolls set out on a chest by someone who had never seen real children. They all had the same face. They all smiled in the same way—politely, patiently—and looked at him with Marysia’s eyes. They smelled of rotten wood and warm earth, sweetly, like the inside of a hollow trunk.
Jaromir looked at his own wrist. Marysia’s ribbon was there, where he had wound it, faded by the dew. The ones in the girls’ hair were new, as if fresh from the fair. Every one of them.
{ skarb_dla_corki:
    Round every neck hung a leather thong with {skarb_jaromira == muszelka:a shell|{skarb_jaromira == pioro:a jay’s feather|a nail}}.
}
His knees went weak. He felt his heart tearing into as many pieces as there were little girls looking up at him from the lichen.
“Papa,” they all said at once, softly, in a single voice. Then such a silence fell that not even the sound of one of them swallowing could be heard.
Then, very far away, beyond the forest, beyond all the trees, someone began the lullaby. It could barely be heard, {pani_w_zbozu_noc == za_spiewem:hoarse, tuneless, the words alone|thin as a thread}, but Jaromir would have known it through a hundred walls. A few of the girls gave a start and looked back over their shoulders in that direction. The others sat motionless and went on smiling. The lullaby settled nothing.
{
- ekwipunek ? szczenie_psa:
    The dog whimpered, began sniffing the air and shifting from paw to paw, first one way, then the other, not knowing which way to run. # pokaz: pies
- pies_pobiegl_sam:
    The russet dog raised his head from under the roots, looked at the girls and at Jaromir—at the stranger in the inside-out coat—and did not get up. # pokaz: pies_spi
}
{ wilk_przy_jaromirze:
    The white wolf rose from the ground and stood by Jaromir’s leg. He never took his eyes off the girls. # pokaz: wilk
- else:
    The white wolf sat upright at the Lord of the Forest’s feet, watching the girls as indifferently as he watched Jaromir. # pokaz: wilk_lesy
}
{ zastaw_u_leszego == zastaw_cien:
    One of the girls cast a shadow—dark, long, broad in the shoulders, far too big for a child. The light came from everywhere and the little ones’ shadows were nothing, but this one lay sharp and clear, like a blot of pitch. # pokaz: cien_duzy
}
“You will touch one,” said the Lord of the Forest. “That one will be yours. There is no second time.”
# pytanie: How will Jaromir know his daughter?
