*   [Hum her the tune.]
    ~ znak_rozpoznania = po_melodii
    He began to hum from the first note, hoarsely, off-key, but he did not stop—that short, strange tune Marysia used to hum to herself before she slept, not Hanka’s lullaby. After a few bars the girls took it up all together, clear and thin, like one voice divided among a dozen throats. # pokaz: spiew
    He did not listen for who was singing. He watched for the one who would close her mouth.
    Halfway through, on the note where it had always broken off, all but one sang on, smoothly, right to the end. That one closed her mouth. She sat third from the left, her lower lip trembling just as it had the time she broke the jug and was afraid someone would shout, and she looked at him, waiting for him to show her how it went. # dalej
