    ~ znak_rozpoznania = po_buzi
    Jaromir went from one to the next, bending over each so low that he felt her breath on his face, taking care not to brush against any of them.
    { wejscie_do_boru == ubranie_na_lewo:
        The dimple—on the left, on the left, he told himself. And all of them had it on the left. All but one. A changeling, he thought, and drew back from her. He chose the one sitting nearest, who had smiled first. Only when he touched her did he glance at the sleeve of his coat, seams outward, and understand that for three days he had been seeing the world the wrong way round. # dalej
        -> zly_wybor
    }
    Freckles, tooth, dimple. Right—right—right. On every one of them the dimple sat on the right side, and the crooked tooth leaned the other way, as if someone had fished a dozen reflections of Marysia out of a pond. Only one had her dimple where it belonged. When he bent towards her, she wrinkled her nose, exactly as she used to when she didn’t want to eat her porridge. # dalej
