~ zapiski += (dzieci_1, pan_lasu_10)
He touched her shoulder.
She was cold, as though only now, after five nights, the chill of the forest had reached her—and she was trembling. Before he could take her in his arms, she burst into loud wailing, her little face red and screwed up, snot under her nose, so ugly and so real that Jaromir laughed through his tears.{ pytanie_do_leszego == gdzie_marysia: “My children never cry,” he remembered. This one was crying for all of them.}
The other girls did not get up. They simply ceased to be: they shrank, turned grey and dropped onto the lichen as handfuls of dry leaves, bark and needles. A wind that was not there swept them into the cleft of the trunk. # pokaz: rozsypane
“You knew her,” said the Lord of the Forest. There was neither anger nor gladness in it. “Take her. No one will stop you. A word for a word.”
Jaromir lifted Marysia. She was lighter than on the day he had last carried her in from the field, and she clung to his neck so tightly he could hardly breathe. She smelled of sour milk, smoke and wet wool—of home. # pokaz: na_rekach
{ skarb_dla_corki:
    She had tangled her fingers in the thong so that they would have had to be unbent one by one.
}
