The other girls did not get up. They simply ceased to be: they shrank, turned grey and dropped onto the lichen as handfuls of dry leaves, bark and needles. The one he held smiled and laid her head on his chest. She was warm. She was light. She did not cry. She did not smell of home—neither of milk nor of smoke. # pokaz: rozsypane
