# tlo: skraj_powrot
Jaromir walked through the forest with the child in his arms, and not once did the paths turn back on themselves. The little one said nothing. She did not ask for her mother, did not complain of being hungry, did not fidget—she only looked at him, patiently and politely, and smiled the same smile each time he glanced down.
From deep in the forest, ever more faintly, someone was humming. It got as far as halfway and fell silent. It did not begin again.
Jaromir did not turn round. He walked on, though he knew already. He was afraid to stop, for then he would have to look.
When he came out at the edge of the young wood and felt the wind from the fields on his face, the child in his arms sighed—once, long, as after a whole day of running about—and grew cold. Her feet were stiff as wood. Her eyes closed of themselves. # pokaz: zimne
{ skarb_dla_corki:
    The thong slipped down into his palm. {skarb_jaromira == muszelka:The shell had a chipped edge and a scratch from the crooked little tooth.|{skarb_jaromira == pioro:The feather was crumpled, its quill bitten.|On the nail sat old brown rust.}} The Lord of the Forest had given the one Jaromir chose the true treasure—so that he would have nothing left to look for.
}
“You will bury it as your own,” he heard once more, though no one stood beside him. # dalej
